where \(\frac{\Delta E}{E}\) is the fractional partonic energy loss and 0.6 is primarily a result of a unitarity correction in the pQCD model [65]. An example of the softening of the fragmentation function is shown in Figure 5.9(b) for a 10 GeV parton in a static source. The high \(z\) depletion of the fragmentation function generates the suppression of high-\(p_{\perp}\) particles in the calculation.

